---
description: Rules for the app server, storage and scheduler
globs: app.py, scheduler/db.py, scheduler/jobs.py, scheduler/web.py, scheduler/notify.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Must run anywhere with only Python or Docker: SQLite in `DATA_DIR`, an in-process scheduler thread, Waitress.
  Don't add external services (Redis, Postgres, cron, cloud queues) or GitHub-based deploys.
- All validation lives in `db.py` (`validate_briefing`, `validate_settings`) and raises `ValidationError`
  with a beginner-friendly message. The API returns it as `{"error": ...}` with status 400.
- Every dashboard/API route uses `login_required` (which checks CSRF on non-GET). `/b/<token>`, `/healthz` and
  `/setup` are the only public routes.
- Secrets: read with `db.get_secret` (env wins). Never return, log or put them in exception text.
- Schema changes need a migration for existing `app.db` files (users upgrade in place).
- Scheduling rules are in AGENTS.md rule 4. `tests/test_jobs.py` covers them, so keep it passing.
- After changes run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest` and, for API/UI changes, `.venv/bin/python qa/e2e.py`.
